  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_002: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), which establishes a weak baseline. The most foundational uncertainty is whether the RNA representation quality (PCA vs. a learned encoder) is a limiting factor, since every downstream multimodal or multiprofile configuration builds on top of the RNA encoder choice. Question: config_008 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_002—only the RNA encoder changes from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200. This isolates the effect of a learned, low-dimensional (200-d) RNA representation versus a high-dimensional (2000-d) linear one. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is the cheapest way to determine whether learned encoders are worth prioritizing in the remaining budget—if scvi_n200 substantially outperforms PCA, I can confidently invest in scvi-based multimodal configs; if they are comparable, the bottleneck lies elsewhere (modality, profile, aggregation) and I should pivot to testing image modality next. (2) It changes exactly one variable relative to the baseline, making the comparison interpretable. (3) scvi_n200 appears in the majority of remaining multimodal configurations, so its standalone performance directly informs which multimodal configs are most promising to test next."
}

